Current Status
Research and architecture phase. All core components are fully specified and documented. A proof of concept implementation of the Mastery Engine is the primary Phase 1 software deliverable.
Prior proof of concept ran on consumer hardware and included:
Constitutional governance layer
Autonomous LoRA training loops
Self-healing architecture
Knowledge graph with 496 nodes and 5,000+ edges
MoE routing across 3B/7B/14B models
Meta-teacher generating its own training data
Development was interrupted by hardware loss and a medical crisis. The architecture survived. Rebuilding now.
Licensing
AxiomOS is dual-licensed:
AGPL-3.0 for open community use
Commercial license for enterprise and SaaS deployment with revenue share back to the commons
All rights reserved during the current pre-licensing period to protect the architecture prior to formal licensing. This is a feature of the design, not a contradiction — the system is built to be open and the licensing will reflect that once properly structured.
Contributing
This project is in pre-founder phase. The governance structure that will manage contributions is itself being built.
If you are interested in becoming a founder contributor — technical, ethical, or verification roles — see the Constitution V1 for role descriptions and the governance philosophy.
Feedback, critique, and architectural challenge are welcome via GitHub issues.
